# Navi cheatsheets

Repo-local sheets live in `cheats/` (on `NAVI_PATH` via devenv `enterShell`).
Global community sheets are [denisidoro/cheats](https://github.com/denisidoro/cheats)
(Home Manager `NAVI_PATH`). Do not copy community sheets into this repo.

## Prefer extend over new files

Before adding `cheats/<topic>.cheat`, open existing sheets and **extend** the
matching `%` tag group (or add cheats under the same tags). New files only when
the topic is clearly separate (e.g. `tests` vs `terminal`).

## Syntax

Follow [navi cheatsheet syntax](https://github.com/denisidoro/navi/blob/master/docs/cheatsheet/syntax/README.md):

```
% tags, here

# One-line description
actual command with <var>

$ var: command that lists suggestions
```

- `%` starts a tag group; `#` description; `$` variable suggestions; `;` comments
- `@` extends another tag group’s variables/context
- Commands must match real scripts/options in this template (`home-switch`,
  `update`, `copier`, devenv tasks, hooks, …) — no invented flags

## Do / do not

```
# ❌ BAD — new file that duplicates home-switch tips already in devenv.cheat
# ✅ GOOD — add another # block under % devenv, bootstrap in cheats/devenv.cheat

# ❌ BAD — generic git tips (use denisidoro/cheats)
# ✅ GOOD — template-specific: commitlint types, tag guard, prek, catalog.toml
```
